{"name":"Parador Inn","hex":"#a99a8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parador","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A simple hotel or bed and breakfast in Spanish-speaking countries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parador"},{"term":"inn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Isinai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any establishment where travellers can procure lodging, food, and drink.","A tavern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parador","blocks":[{"text":"A parador, in Spain and other Spanish-speaking countries was an establishment where travelers could seek lodging, and usually, food and drink, similar to an inn. In Spain since 1928, a Parador is a state-owned luxury hotel, usually located in a converted historic building such as a monastery or castle, or in a place of natural beauty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/El_patio_de_un_parador_%28Museo_del_Prado%29.jpg/330px-El_patio_de_un_parador_%28Museo_del_Prado%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parador","wikidata":"Q42899902"},{"title":"Inn","blocks":[{"text":"Inns are generally establishments or buildings where travelers can seek lodging, and usually, food and drink. Inns are typically located in the country or along a highway. Before the advent of motorized transportation, they also provided accommodation for horses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/King_George_Inn.JPG/330px-King_George_Inn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inn","wikidata":"Q256020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Roadside-inn-American-scenery.jpeg/500px-Roadside-inn-American-scenery.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&